{
	title: 'Typed commands outrank passive completion; outside interaction dismisses',
	spec: 'Restore these invariants: passive autocomplete never substitutes a suggestion for a fully typed registered slash command, and a completion menu does not remain orphaned after focus leaves its interaction area. In the web command composer, plain Enter submits the original typed text when its command name exactly matches a registered command, regardless of arguments, passive highlighting, menu timing or candidate ordering. Thus /cd runs bare, /cd with an existing path submits that path, and /cd with a missing path reaches the command creation question. Do not normalize paths or validate arguments in the completion UI. For an incomplete command name, Enter accepts the highlighted completion without submitting. Explicit Up/Down menu navigation makes Enter accept that choice without submitting; editing the input resets that intent, and host replies cannot manufacture it. Tab and clicking a choice still accept without submitting; Shift/Alt Enter and touch keyboard behavior retain their existing contracts. The Enter hint reflects whether it sends or chooses. Terminal submission keeps its existing behavior. A pointer/touch interaction outside the message editor and completion popup dismisses the completion menu without changing typed text, selecting a suggestion, blocking the outside action or forcing focus back. Keyboard focus leaving this interaction area also dismisses it. Escape dismisses an open completion menu even when focus is outside the editor, without also pausing the session. Dismissal suppresses late replies for unchanged input; new editing can request fresh suggestions. Preserve keyboard access and popup choice clicks. Cover command Enter, explicit selection reset, stale replies, and outside/focus dismissal with focused behavioral regressions. Pointer activation of a completion, including iOS taps, keeps editor focus until click accepts the choice; a transient blur must not remove the popup before activation. Selection fills the draft without submitting. Touch scrolling or cancellation must not select a choice.',
	status: 'done',
	notes: [
		'Completion receive deliberately reuses identical menus across inputs. Reset explicit arrow intent before prediction, not in host reply handling, so passive replies cannot create intent and edits cannot retain it. Keep intent only while the selected candidate survives. Use the registered command name only; send original arguments through the existing submit path without filesystem checks.',
		'Dismissal clears pending Tab intent as well as cached choices and suppresses unchanged-input replies even before a popup appears. Pointer and focus listeners scope the interaction to the textarea and popup (not Send/Attach); focus within the popup preserves native choice clicks. Touch Enter bypasses menu acceptance so the existing native newline contract holds.',
		'On iOS, a tapped native button need not receive focus. The composer focusout listener therefore treated the textarea blur as outside interaction and removed the completion before click. Prevent pointerdown default on choices to retain editor focus; leave selection on click so touch scrolling/cancellation cannot accept a candidate and keyboard activation still uses the native button.',
		'The browser regression models Safari blur-without-button-focus, checks cancellation preserves the editor and draft, and uses a trusted Chromium touch tap to verify click still selects without submission. It fails without focus retention. Physical iOS keyboard behavior remains unverified.',
		'Keyboard navigation keeps the selected completion row fully visible by scrolling only the suggestion panel, including Up/Down wraparound. Input focus, composer position and conversation reading position stay unchanged.',
		'iPhone 2026-11-11: tapping a /model completion left the draft unchanged and closed the keyboard; iOS ended the touch without click, as for composer actions (qp9). Choices now share the qp9 tap handler: a touch lifted inside chooses at pointerup, a click within 1 s after is ignored, and the stray-click guard covers choices. Invariant: one tap on a choice fills the draft on iOS. Browser test fails at HEAD, passes with the fix; not yet confirmed on an iPhone.'
	],
	needs: ['1b']
